#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""watchctl — the one-command USB/WiFi debug rig for the esp32c6-watch fleet.

Closes the two chronic tooling holes:
  #20 the SLOT TRAP  — bare `espflash flash` writes ota_0 while otadata boots
                       ota_1; `watchctl deploy` always writes the BOOTING slot.
  #21 the USB WEDGE  — the C6 USB-Serial-JTAG recurrently wedges; `watchctl
                       reset|recover` walk the proven recovery ladder.

Watches are ALWAYS addressed by sigil or efuse-MAC serial, never by ttyACM
number (ttyACM numbers shuffle on every replug).

    watchctl list                                   # fleet presence + ports
    watchctl logs eldritch-lantern --seconds 20     # capture serial output
    watchctl logs mythic-throne --reset             # boot burst (panic capture)
    watchctl reset eldritch-lantern                 # verified reset (+ ladder)
    watchctl recover eldritch-lantern               # the full wedge ladder
    watchctl slot mythic-throne                     # booting slot + fingerprint
    watchctl deploy eldritch-lantern fw.elf         # slot-trap-proof deploy
    watchctl flash-full mythic-throne fw.elf --erase-otadata   # provisioning
    watchctl console eldritch-lantern               # debug-console REPL
    watchctl test eldritch-lantern hotpaths         # ui_test.py suites
    watchctl ota-status                             # ubox0 journal + announce
    watchctl endpoint eldritch-lantern              # WiFi debug endpoint probe

Global flags: --json (machine output), --transport usb|wifi|auto, -v.
Exit codes:   0 ok · 2 not-found/usage · 3 recovery-needed · 4 gate-failed.

Dependencies: python3 stdlib; pyserial if available (falls back to a raw
termios tty). espflash for flash/reset operations (~/.cargo/bin/espflash).

The full field guide lives in docs/debugging.md.
"""

